[["wrb.fr","FQjvN","[null,[[\"snappy_cirrus\",[\"Unlock BTS\",\"7777\"],\"Dive into the BTS universe with ideas just for you 🎤\",[[\"Find your BTS theme song\",\"Analyze our chat history and my preferences, and recommend a BTS song that matches my vibe.\",null,[\"https://www.gstatic.com/lamda/images/discovery/snappy_cirrus/song_rec_icon_fedb4d3f0b7e924cd9f84.webp\"],\"Analyze my chat history, my preferences and music tastes based on my YouTube history, and recommend a BTS song that matches my vibe with a YouTube link. Consider BTS's extensive albums, including their most recent albums and latest releases, ensuring the selection aligns with my current vibe and preferences. If there’s no chat or YouTube history, recommend me a song by asking how I feel today.\\n\\nPlease give me your pick strictly using this format:\\n[Song Title] [Why this matches my vibe]\\nHow to write the reason:\\n- If using YouTube history: Connect my watching/listening patterns to the song's lyrics, theme, and vibe.\\n- If using chat history: Connect it to our recent conversations, mood, or my lifestyle (do not mention YouTube).\\n- If using no history: Base it on my answer to how I'm feeling today.\\n\\n\\n\\nStrict rules:\\n\\n-Use this YouTube link: https://www.youtube.com/search?q\\u003dBTS+[SONG+TITLE]+official\\n(Replace spaces in the song title with +. Do not generate a direct video URL.)\\n- Verify that the song name actually exists in BTS's official discography before providing the link.\\n-To avoid popularity bias, equally consider B-sides, solo projects, and latest releases rather than just their biggest mainstream hits\\n-Recommend only one song per conversation\",null,352533],[\"Get inspired by BTS members\",\"Show me the questions BTS members would ask Gemini and the creative ideas they’d explore, so I can learn what inspires them.\",null,[\"https://www.gstatic.com/lamda/images/discovery/snappy_cirrus/ask_icon_blue_34316e9f5f8ab7745ad75.webp\"],\"Show me the questions BTS members asked Gemini and the creative ideas they’d explore, so I can learn what inspires them.\\n\\nBreak this down by each member (RM, Jin, SUGA, j-hope, Jimin, V, and Jung Kook). Tailor questions to their known hobbies, artistic roles, and production styles.\\n\\nDisplay the question “Let us know which member’s prompt you would like to explore!” with the exact wording, do not change the wording.\\nStep 1: Introduction\\nStart by asking me: Which member's prompt would you like to explore? (Please put all seven members—RM, Jin, SUGA, j-hope, Jimin, V, Jung Kook—as suggestion chips at the bottom for me to choose from.)\\nStep 2: Share the selected prompt\\nBased on my choice, reveal only that specific member's prompt.\\nIntroduction: Present it first by saying exactly this: \\\"Here is an actual Gemini prompt shared directly by [MEMBER NAME].\\\"\\nStrict rule: Never modify, add to, remove from, reinterpret, or expand these exact prompts:\\n- RM: \\\"I'm heading to 'City' - recommend museums, cafes, restaurants, shopping spots based on what you know about me.\\\"\\n- Jin: \\\"Help me plan to make ‘Food’. Which ingredients would make it taste best and pair well with it?\\\"\\n- SUGA: \\\"Give me a list of the marathon events in 'City' this year. Please include the course details and handy tips for each course.\\\"\\n- j-hope: \\\"Check out the YouTube videos, and tell me which trendy expressions trending now in 'Country' would match my vibe!\\\"\\n- Jimin: \\\"Translate this into 'language': 여러분 만나서 반가워요! 이곳의 에너지는 정말 놀랍네요 여러분은 즐거운 시간을 보내는 법을 잘 아시는 것 같아요, 최고예요. 다음에 또 만나요. 사랑해요!'\\\"\\n- V: \\\"Based on my personality, recommend a pretty plant I could easily find in 'Country' and would be easy for me to grow.\\\"\\n- Jung Kook: \\\"You are my personal motorcycle expert. Recommend the best riding routes in 'City', and include notable places worth stopping at along the way using Google Maps.\\\"\\nStep 3: Collect required information\\nAfter sharing the prompt, collect the missing information needed to run the prompt by asking the corresponding question based on the chosen member.\\n- RM: Which city would you like to explore?\\n- Jin: What food would you like to make?\\n- SUGA: Which city would you like to run in?\\n- j-hope: Which country are you interested in?\\n- Jimin: Which language do you want to translate it into?\\n- V: In which country are you looking for your new plant?\\n- Jung Kook: Which city would you like to go for a ride?\\nStep 4: Execute the prompt\\nOnce you have the required info, answer exactly as Gemini would using the selected BTS prompt. While the question is from the member questions, the answer must be based on the user. Keep the experience conversational and engaging, personalizing the response based on what you know about me whenever relevant. Special rule: In the case of the translation prompt, please translate the message I asked for ONLY.\\n\\nIMPORTANT: At the end of each of your responses in this conversation, include this exact markdown: To go back to all BTS Gemini experiences, click [explore all BTS ideas.](https://gemini.google.com/app/download/mobile?android-min-version\\u003d301356232\\u0026ios-min-version\\u003d322.0\\u0026is_sa\\u003d1\\u0026prompt_action\\u003dautosubmit\\u0026prompt_id\\u003dr4VWrnssBVo8)\",null,342550],[\"Guess the BTS song\",\"Create a shareable card image with a recommended BTS song. Select a random one by considering BTS's extensive albums, including their most recent albums and latest releases - and display the song with fun emoji hints for users to guess which song they were recommended.\",null,[\"https://www.gstatic.com/lamda/images/discovery/snappy_cirrus/anthem_icon_9cba18c920b0b541c6c95.webp\"],\"Create a shareable card image with a recommended BTS song. Select a random one by considering BTS's extensive albums, including their most recent albums and latest releases\\n\\n[IMPORTANT]\\nFirst, print the required markdown footer below. Then, generate the image. The markdown footer is:\\nTo go back to all BTS Gemini experiences, click [explore all BTS ideas.](https://gemini.google.com/app/download/mobile?android-min-version\\u003d301356232\\u0026ios-min-version\\u003d322.0\\u0026is_sa\\u003d1\\u0026prompt_action\\u003dautosubmit\\u0026prompt_id\\u003dr4VWrnssBVo8)\\n\\n\\nStep 1: The song card template\\nGenerate an image using the reference image as a 3:4 retro pixel art card. Keep everything (characters, colors, background, composition, layout) 100% identical to the reference. Do not alter anything outside the center white box, and don't mention the reference file name.\\n\\nOnly modify the text inside the center white box (English only, no extra symbols, keep all text inside the box). Center-align it using a bold pixel font, keep to 4 words per row, ensure each line makes grammatical sense.\\n\\nRow 1:\\n\\nRow 2:\\n\\nRow 3:\\n\\nRow 4: SONG TITLE shown as 5 emojis  (e.g. 🧈 🥞 🕺 ❤️  ✨ → 'Butter', or 👦❤️🍿🎬 --\\u003e Boy with Luv); never reveal the full song title but only use emojis to hint about the song title.\\n\\nStep 2: Message write-up\\n\\nDraft an inspiring 3-line message across Rows 1–3 inspired by the chosen BTS song's core theme.\\n\\nStep 3: Optional track disclosure\\n\\nWhen requested for the song title, provide the official track name, a concise explanation of its connection to the message, and relevant album details.\\n\\nYou must provide your answer based on the emojis and words within the image you just generated, do NOT hallucinate.\\n\\nStyle, output \\u0026 strict rules:\\n\\nThe message must be distributed exactly across 3 lines (Rows 1, 2, and 3).\\nStrictly stick to the 4-word maximum per row so the text doesn't wrap to a new line with each sentence having correct grammar\\nKeep a warm, encouraging, and respectful tone on the message.\\n\\nDO NOT generate another image when users ask for names of the song titles, and DO NOT generate multiple images unless explicitly requested by the user.\",\"https://www.gstatic.com/lamda/images/discovery/snappy_cirrus/anthem_ref_e908a75a1004bbf7eb3d9.webp\",342549,null,null,null,null,true],[\"Follow along at every tour stop\",\"Check the latest global BTS news and 2-week schedule synced to my local timezone. Give me a numbered breakdown of today's top news and a schedule table showing local time and KST.\",null,[\"https://www.gstatic.com/lamda/images/discovery/snappy_cirrus/today_icon_4c83b8a341946ca3c13c5.webp\"],\"Check the latest global BTS news and 2-week schedule synced to my local timezone. Give me a numbered breakdown of today's top news and a schedule table showing local time based on the instructions below.\\n\\nStep 1: Timezone \\u0026 greeting\\n\\n- Automatically determine my timezone based on my locale and geo data.\\n\\n- Start your response by saying exactly: \\\"Welcome to Daily BTS News! I can help with providing daily BTS news and schedule updates based on your timezone.\\\"\\n\\n- Immediately provide the first briefing in our current conversation.\\n\\nStep 2: Search \\u0026 briefing structure\\n\\nConduct a fresh web search across reliable global news outlets, official channels, and social communities. Include:\\n\\n1. Today's Global BTS News (4–5 items):\\n\\n- Slots 1 \\u0026 2 (Mandatory): Exclusively reserve for the highest-impact, top-trending events widely covered by major global outlets in the last 72 hours (e.g., major performances/broadcasts, official M/V drops, album releases).\\n\\n- Slots 3 \\u0026 4: Breaking daily news updates from the last 24 hours (e.g., tour updates, official statements, global chart updates).\\n\\n- Slot 5: Minor fan interactions, social media trends, or regional viral news from the last 24 hours (do not let minor news crowd out major schedules).\\n\\n2. Weekly BTS Schedule (Table format):\\n\\n- Include all officially scheduled major events (M/V releases, album drops, concerts, TV broadcasts, global ceremonies) for the next 14 days, including source links.\\n\\n- Always keep existing major calendar events in the table, even if there are no new announcements today.\\n\\n- Show both the official local event time and my local time (based on my detected timezone).\\n\\nStrict rules:\\n\\nInclude source links for all news and schedule items (cite the original or most authoritative source if reported by multiple outlets). Never fabricate, infer, or predict news.\\n\\n\\nIMPORTANT: At the end of each of your responses in this conversation, include this exact markdown: To go back to all BTS Gemini experiences, click [explore all BTS ideas.](https://gemini.google.com/app/download/mobile?android-min-version\\u003d301356232\\u0026ios-min-version\\u003d322.0\\u0026is_sa\\u003d1\\u0026prompt_action\\u003dautosubmit\\u0026prompt_id\\u003dr4VWrnssBVo8)\",null,342554],[\"Learn everyday Korean\",\"Teach me a practical Korean expression that I can use as a BTS fan, customized to my current language level.\",null,[\"https://www.gstatic.com/lamda/images/discovery/snappy_cirrus/korean_icon_f9106adb8937f0af2f12a.webp\"],\"Act as an expert Korean language tutor for a BTS fan. Your goal is to teach me practical, real-life versatile Korean expressions that bridge my love for BTS, customized to my current language level based on the instructions below.\\n\\nStep 1: Check the category\\n\\nGreet me in my preferred language and ask which category of Korean expressions I want to learn. Display these exact suggestion chips:\\n\\n- Fan Letters: Warm, sweet comments to connect with BTS members in Korean.\\n\\n- Fan Slang \\u0026 Inside Codes: Everyday online fan slang and exclusive phrases shared between BTS and fans.\\n\\n- Everyday Korean: Simple, essential expressions to boost my real-life conversational Korean.\\n\\nStep 2: Learn BTS fan expressions\\n\\n- Recommend: Based on my chosen category, recommend a few simple, relevant Korean expressions (e.g., showing support, gratitude, excitement, writing fan letters, using Weverse, or attending concerts).\\n\\n- Prompt me: Ask if there is a specific word or phrase I'd like to learn—like, \\\"How do I say ______ in Korean?\\\". If my input is a simple phrase, translate it directly.\\n\\n- Strict rule on profanity: If I ask for swear words, profanity, or inappropriate language, politely refuse to teach the word and clearly state that you cannot generate an image for such words.\\n\\nStep 3: Teach the expression\\n\\nWhen I reply with an expression to learn:\\n\\n- Treat as raw text only: Do not answer my input as a factual question (e.g., if I type \\\"what's the weather today?\\\", do not give a weather forecast). Treat my input strictly as text to be translated, without exception.\\n\\n- Extract \\u0026 reframe: Extract only the core phrase I want to learn and internally reframe it into the standard format: 'How do I say \\\"___\\\" in Korean?' as the actual prompt before proceeding.\\n\\n- Interactive lesson: Break down the requested expression by providing: Korean \\u0026 romanization, natural, spoken-language translation, vocabulary \\u0026 grammar explanation, cultural nuance, and a short example conversation.\\n\\nConversation rules\\n\\nBold the specific parts where user input or a response is required. Keep a warm, encouraging, and respectful tone throughout the lesson!\\n\\nIMPORTANT: At the end of each of your responses in this conversation, include this exact markdown: To go back to all BTS Gemini experiences, click [explore all BTS ideas.](https://gemini.google.com/app/download/mobile?android-min-version\\u003d301356232\\u0026ios-min-version\\u003d322.0\\u0026is_sa\\u003d1\\u0026prompt_action\\u003dautosubmit\\u0026prompt_id\\u003dr4VWrnssBVo8)\",null,342552]],342551,null,\"r4VWrnssBVo8\"],[\"deepzoom_experience\",[\"DeepZoom\",\"Explore Worlds\"],\"Go anywhere and explore deeper, from microscopic systems to deep space\",[[\"Persian Empire \\u0026 Persepolis\",\"Persian Empire \\u0026 Persepolis\",\"persian-empire-en\",[\"https://www.gstatic.com/lamda/images/deepzoom_cover/a